#org @gText_BattleFrontier_RulesPrompt
What would you like to know\nabout the [BUFFER1]?

#org @gText_BattleFrontier_ChoiceFrontierRules
Frontier Rules

#org @gText_BattleFrontier_ChoiceFacilityRules
Facility Rules

#org @gText_BattleFrontier_CommonRules
At the Battle Frontier, you'll take\non challengers one after another.\pEvery Pok\emon battles at level 50\nand is healed before each fight.\pAs you win, your streak will grow\nand you'll face stronger trainers.\pYou'll earn Pok\e Chips for each win.\nJust remember you can only hold\lup to 999 Pok\e Chips at a time!\pIf you ever need a break, you can\nRest - we'll save your streak and\lhold it until you return.\pPlease make sure to complete a\nbattle before resting - otherwise\lyour streak will be lost!

#org @gText_BattleFrontier_TowerRules
The Battle Tower emphasizes\ntraditionl battles - no gimmicks.\pJust you, your team, and one\nchallenger after another.

#org @gText_BattleFrontier_QuarryRules
In the Battle Quarry, the rock face\nshifts before every turn.\pIt seals off two of the four move\nslots of every Pok\emon in the pit.\pBoth sides are sealed. If a Pok\emon\ncannot act, it must Struggle.

#org @gText_BattleFrontier_SimRules
The Battle Sim runs every battle as\na simulation, and no two are alike.\pBefore each one, the machines roll a\nnew set of conditions for the field.\pThe longer your streak, the more\nconditions they will stack on.

#org @gText_BattleFrontier_MazeRules
In the Battle Maze, you're handed a\nrandom team to battle with.\pThis team is built from the same pool\nyour opponents may have.\pYour team is changed after every\nbattle.\pThere is nothing to prepare for this\nfacility - just do your best!

#org @gText_BattleFrontier_FactoryRules
At the Battle Factory, you rent a\nteam to battle with from us.\pI'll lay out six Pok\emon, drawn from\nthe same pool as your opponents.\pYou choose which of them to enter,\nand they are yours for the run.\pAfter every win, you may trade one\nof yours for one you just faced.\pIf you choose to rest, the team you\nwere using is used when you return.

#org @gText_BattleFrontier_IsleRules
Battles at the Battle Isle are\nfought in the traditional way.\pHeld items and abilities do not\nactiavate.\pMega Evolution and Z-Moves have no\nplace here either.\pAll moves are physical or special\nbased on their type.

#org @gText_BattleFrontier_ObservatoryRules
The Battle Observatory hosts a\nseries of duels between battlers.\pYou and your opponent reveal every\nPok\emon you brought.\pStudy your opponent, then choose\nyour Pok\emon to duel with.\pDuels are 1v1 in singles, and 2v2\nin doubles.\pDuel with honour! Mega Evolution and\nZ- Moves are not permitted.

#org @gText_BattleFrontier_ObservatoryReveal
The observatory lights come up on\nboth teams!\pYour opponent revealed [BUFFER1],\n[BUFFER2] and [BUFFER3]!

// Doubles reveals four Pokemon and there are only three buffers, so the last two share one - and
// it has to be BUFFER1, the only one wide enough to hold a pair. Hence the out-of-order reads:
// BUFFER2 is the first Pokemon, BUFFER3 the second, BUFFER1 the third and fourth together.
#org @gText_BattleFrontier_ObservatoryRevealDouble
The observatory lights come up on\nboth teams!\pYour opponent revealed [BUFFER2],\n[BUFFER3], [BUFFER1]!

#org @gText_ObservatoryNameJoiner
 and 

#org @gText_BattleFrontier_ObservatoryOfferLook
Would you like a closer look at\ntheir team?

#org @gText_BattleFrontier_ObservatoryChoosePrompt
Which Pok\emon will you send out?

#org @gText_BattleFrontier_ObservatoryChoosePromptDouble
Which two Pok\emon will you send out?

#org @gText_BattleFrontier_ObservatoryPlayerChoice
You chose [BUFFER1]!

#org @gText_BattleFrontier_ObservatoryPlayerChoiceDouble
You chose [BUFFER1] and [BUFFER2]!

#org @gText_BattleFrontier_ObservatoryOpponentChoice
Your opponent chose [BUFFER1]!

#org @gText_BattleFrontier_ObservatoryOpponentChoiceDouble
Your opponent chose [BUFFER1]\nand [BUFFER2]!

#org @gText_BattleFrontier_ObservatoryBattleStarting
Let the duel begin!

#org @gText_BattleFrontier_SandsRules
In the Battle Sands, you put your\ntrust in your Pok\emon.\pYou choose if they fight or switch,\nbut they choose their own moves.\pWhenever a Pok\emon enters battle,\nthey are empowered by the sands.\pThis raises a random stat, with the\nintensity growing with your streak.

//------------------------------------------------------------------
// Choosing a format and entering a team
//------------------------------------------------------------------

#org @gText_BattleFrontier_ChooseFormat
Which format would you like to\nchallenge?

#org @gText_BattleFrontier_ChoiceSingles
Singles

#org @gText_BattleFrontier_ChoiceDoubles
Doubles

// Swapped in for the two above when that format has a run waiting to be picked back up.

#org @gText_BattleFrontier_ChoiceSinglesOnHold
Singles (on hold)

#org @gText_BattleFrontier_ChoiceDoublesOnHold
Doubles (on hold)

#org @gText_BattleFrontier_ConfirmChallenge
The [BUFFER2] format? That will\nrequire [BUFFER3] Pok\emon to enter.\pIs that okay?

// Shown for the Battle Maze, since the player doesn't bring their own Pokemon
#org @gText_BattleFrontier_ConfirmChallengeRandom
The [BUFFER2] format? I'll give you\n[BUFFER3] Pok\emon per battle.\pIs that okay?

#org @gText_BattleFrontier_ChooseTeam
Please choose the Pok\emon you'd\nlike to enter.

// Shown for the Battle Factory, which lays out a pool and lets the player choose 3/4 from there
#org @gText_BattleFrontier_ConfirmChallengeRental
The [BUFFER2] format? I'll provide six\nPok\emon for you to choose from.\pYou'll enter [BUFFER3] of them.\nIs that okay?

#org @gText_BattleFrontier_FactoryChooseRentals
Here are your options. Please choose\nthe ones you'd like to rent.

#org @gText_BattleFrontier_FactorySwapPrompt
You may swap one of your Pok\emon\nwith one your opponent had.\pWould you like to swap?

#org @gText_BattleFrontier_FactorySwapChooseOwn
Which of your Pok\emon will you\ngive up?

#org @gText_BattleFrontier_FactorySwapChooseTheirs
And which of theirs would you\nlike to take?

#org @gText_BattleFrontier_FactorySwapDone
Done! [BUFFER1] has gone with your\nopponent, and [BUFFER2] joins you.

#org @gText_BattleFrontier_FactorySwapDeclined
Very well - you'll continue with\nthe team you have.

//------------------------------------------------------------------
// Walking to and from the battle area
//------------------------------------------------------------------
#org @gText_BattleFrontier_LeadToBattlePosition
Please follow me, and we'll get your\nchallenge started.

#org @gText_BattleFrontier_SandsLeadToArena
Step up to the sands, please.

#org @gText_BattleFrontier_LeadToLobby
Let me lead you out of the battle\nspace. Right this way.

#org @gText_BattleFrontier_SimCalibrating
Hold still - the simulator is\ncalibrating the field[.]

// gStringVarC is filled in by sp072. Its descriptions are written to follow this exact prefix, so do not reword the first line.
#org @gText_BattleFrontier_SimEffectRolled
The next battle will take place\n[BUFFER][0C]

#org @gText_BattleFrontier_CallingOpponent
We'll call your next opponent in\nnow.

//------------------------------------------------------------------
// Battles
//------------------------------------------------------------------

// Fallbacks only - in a Frontier battle the engine prints the opponent's own lines from the trainer table instead of these.
#org @gText_BattleFrontier_OpponentDefeated
I couldn't keep up with you!

#org @gText_BattleFrontier_OpponentVictorious
Better luck next time!

#org @gText_BattleFrontier_AttendantWin
Congratulations on your win!

#org @gText_BattleFrontier_AttendantWinMilestone
Incredible! Overcoming such a\npowerful trainer is no small feat.

#org @gText_BattleFrontier_AttendantLoss
Oh dear[.] This loss has ended your\nchallenge.

#org @gText_BattleFrontier_WinReward
That's [BUFFER3] straight in the\n[BUFFER1]!\pHere are [BUFFER2] Pok\e Chips for\nyour trouble.

#org @gText_BattleFrontier_WinRewardCaseFull
That's [BUFFER3] straight in the\n[BUFFER1]!\pYou'll have to spend some Pok\e Chips\nto make room for more!

//------------------------------------------------------------------
// Continue / Rest / Give up
//------------------------------------------------------------------

#org @gText_BattleFrontier_ChallengeMenuPrompt
Your [BUFFER1] [BUFFER2]\nstreak stands at [BUFFER3].\pWould you like to continue?

// The two below replace the prompt above when a milestone battle is next, so the player is never surprised into one - see FrontierChallenge_GetNextOpponentKind.
#org @gText_BattleFrontier_ChallengeMenuPromptAce
Your [BUFFER1] [BUFFER2]\nstreak stands at [BUFFER3].\pA word of warning - an especially\nstrong Trainer is next up.\pWould you like to continue?

#org @gText_BattleFrontier_ChallengeMenuPromptBrain
Your [BUFFER1] [BUFFER2]\nstreak stands at [BUFFER3].\pWaiting in the next room is\nthe master of the [BUFFER1]\lthemselves!\pWould you like to continue?

#org @gText_BattleFrontier_ChoiceContinue
Continue

#org @gText_BattleFrontier_ChoiceRest
Rest

#org @gText_BattleFrontier_ChoiceAbandon
Give up

#org @gText_BattleFrontier_ConfirmRest
We'll save your progress and hold\nyour streak until you come back\lfor it.\pYou're free to go wherever you\nlike in the meantime - even to\lanother facility.\pWould you like to Rest?

#org @gText_BattleFrontier_Resting
We'll be waiting for you!

//------------------------------------------------------------------
// Picking a run back up
//------------------------------------------------------------------

#org @gText_BattleFrontier_WelcomeBackRested
Your [BUFFER2] streak of [BUFFER3]\nis currently on hold.\pFeel free to bring a different\nteam this time, if you like.

// Variant for the Maze and Factory, which hand the player their team
#org @gText_BattleFrontier_WelcomeBackRestedProvidedTeam
Your [BUFFER2] streak of [BUFFER3]\nis currently on hold.

#org @gText_BattleFrontier_OnHoldMenuPrompt
What would you like to do with it?

// Variant for when a player resumes before an Ace/Brain
#org @gText_BattleFrontier_OnHoldMenuPromptSpecial
Before you decide - an especially\nstrong Trainer is up next.\pWhat would you like to do?

#org @gText_BattleFrontier_OnHoldMenuPromptBrain
Before you decide - waiting in the\nnext room is the master of the\l[BUFFER1] themselves.\pWhat would you like to do?

#org @gText_BattleFrontier_ChoiceKeepOnHold
Nothing

#org @gText_BattleFrontier_ResumeWarning
Understood.\pJust remember[.] Once the next battle\nbegins, you'll have to see it\lthrough.\pStopping partway will cost you\nyour streak.\pWith that said, let's begin[.]

#org @gText_BattleFrontier_ConfirmAbandon
Giving up will end your run, and\nyour [BUFFER1] [BUFFER2]\lstreak of [BUFFER3] will be lost.\pAre you sure?

#org @gText_BattleFrontier_Abandoned
Thank you for challenging the\n[BUFFER1]!\pWe hope to see you again.

#org @gText_BattleFrontier_Lost
Your [BUFFER1] challenge\nhas come to an end.\pThank you for battling, and please\ncome again!
